# Review Rounds

> **Purpose**
>
> Review Rounds represent a complete review iteration during the lifecycle of a Task.
>
> Every time work is submitted for review, a Review Round is created (or continued) to maintain complete traceability of reviews, feedback, deliverables, approvals, and implementation history.
>
> Review Rounds allow the system to answer questions such as:
>
> - How many times was this asset reviewed?
> - What changed between reviews?
> - Which feedback belonged to each review cycle?
> - Which deliverable version was approved?

---

# Overview

A Review Round groups together every artifact generated during a review cycle.

A Review Round contains:

- Reviews
- Feedback Items
- Deliverable Versions
- Review Decisions
- Review Attachments
- Review Discussions
- Linked SubTasks
- Timeline Events

---

# Objectives

Review Rounds provide:

- Complete review history
- Production traceability
- Version comparison
- Client communication history
- Rework analysis
- Approval history
- Audit compliance

---

# Architecture

```text
Production

↓

Review Round

├── Review(s)
├── Feedback
├── Deliverables
├── Discussions
├── Decisions
└── Timeline

↓

Production

↓

Next Review Round
```

---

# Round Lifecycle

```text
Created

↓

Review Started

↓

Feedback

↓

Implementation

↓

Verification

↓

Completed
```

If another review is required:

↓

New Review Round

---

# Review Round Numbering

Each Task maintains its own numbering.

Example

```
Task PM-1024

Round 1

Round 2

Round 3

Round 4
```

Round numbers are never reused.

---

# Review Types within a Round

One Round may contain multiple review stages.

Example

```
Round 3

↓

Lead Review

↓

Final Review

↓

QC

↓

Client Review
```

---

# Deliverables

Each Round references one or more deliverables.

Example

```
Round 2

↓

Version 1.2

↓

Version 1.3

↓

Version 1.4
```

---

# Feedback Association

Every Feedback Item belongs to exactly one Review Round.

Example

```
Round 2

↓

Feedback 101

Feedback 102

Feedback 103
```

Round 3 creates new Feedback Items.

---

# SubTask Association

SubTasks created from Feedback record:

- Review Round
- Feedback Source
- SubTask Type

Example

```
Round 2

↓

Feedback

↓

Lead Analysis

↓

FR Fix Task
```

---

# Round Decisions

Possible outcomes

- Approved
- Minor Fix
- Major Fix
- Rejected
- Cancelled

---

# Round Completion

A Review Round is completed when:

- All Reviews finished
- Feedback recorded
- Decision finalized

Implementation may continue after completion.

---

# Round History

Each Round stores:

- Round Number
- Started On
- Completed On
- Reviewer(s)
- Decision
- Deliverables
- Feedback Count
- SubTask Count

History is immutable.

---

# Review Progression

Example

```text
Round 1

↓

Major Fix

↓

Production

↓

Round 2

↓

Minor Fix

↓

Production

↓

Round 3

↓

Approved
```

